# Hosts that reject GitHub-hosted runners rather than being genuinely broken.
# Verified by hand: each returns 200 from a normal client but fails from CI, so
# checking them produces a weekly false-positive report instead of signal.
# Re-test before removing an entry — these are environment quirks, not permanent truths.

# oreilly.com serves 403 to every non-interactive client, including a request carrying a
# browser User-Agent, so this is not a runner-IP problem that a retry or a header would fix.
# The two entries in philosophy.md's further-reading list are book landing pages that resolve
# normally in a browser.
https://www\.oreilly\.com/.*
